        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: University of California, San Francisco; Pennsylvania State University; University of California system\n- People: Laurence S. Baskin; Greg Huntington\n- Places: San Francisco, California; Pennsylvania\n- Roles: professor of pediatrics; chief of pediatric urology; college football player\n- Events: founding; university affiliation; 1993 NFL Draft\n\nFacts:\n- Pennsylvania State University was founded in 1855.\n- The University of California, San Francisco was founded as Toland Medical College in 1864.\n- The University of California, San Francisco became affiliated with the University of California in 1873.\n- Greg Huntington played college football at Penn State University and was drafted in the fifth round of the 1993 NFL Draft.\n- The University of California, San Francisco is a research university in San Francisco, California, and it is part of the University of California system.\n- Pennsylvania State University is a state-related, land-grant, doctoral university with campuses and facilities throughout Pennsylvania.\n- Pennsylvania State University states a threefold mission of teaching, research, and public service.\n- Laurence S. Baskin is a professor of pediatrics and chief of pediatric urology at the University of California, San Francisco.",
